# Playwright for the browser smoke test — installed per-run in CI with
# `npm install --no-save`, and the same way locally. Never committed.
node_modules/

__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# Raw source snapshots — kept as workflow artifacts, never committed
# (the Redfin tracker alone is ~1.5GB). See docs/DATA.md.
archive/

# Supabase CLI local state (written by `supabase link` / `functions deploy`).
# Machine-specific, and the CLI also caches credentials here on some flows —
# never commit it.
supabase/.temp/

# Vendor-derived records pulled out of the public repo (Prompt 1). RETAINED,
# not deleted — legal review wants retention, so this is moved to private
# storage by hand rather than removed. Never commit it back.
_private_data_export/

# Generated at deploy time by pipeline/provision_readings.py from the
# committed page manifest, plus readings for released tranches pulled from the
# private store. Was committed source carrying per-ZIP vendor metrics for
# 28,000+ ZIPs — and because the whole of web/ is the deployed artifact, it
# was also a public bulk-download endpoint at /data/zips/{ST}.json regardless
# of whether any page linked it.
web/data/z/

# Generated at deploy time by pipeline/build_pages.py from committed web/data.
# ~18.6k pages / 147MB — never committed (9.8MB gzipped in the Pages artifact).
web/zip/
web/sitemaps/
web/sitemap.xml
web/robots.txt
web/llms.txt
web/og/

web/verdict-copy.js
web/s/

# Generated at deploy time by pipeline/build_research.py from committed
# pipeline/research JSONs — pages, charts, CSVs.
web/research/

# Generated at deploy time by pipeline/post_pack.py from the committed
# pack manifest — one card per marketing task. Public by design (they are
# destined for public feeds) but never committed: they are re-rendered from
# the manifest on every deploy, deterministically.
web/assets/mkt/

# Generated at deploy time by pipeline/post_pack.py — one static redirect
# per marketing task, so the short link in a caption carries the campaign
# token the nightly performance join reads.
web/go/

# Generated at deploy time by pipeline/build_metro.py — one page per metro
# area, plus the hub and the /methodology short route.
web/metro/

# Generated at deploy time by pipeline/build_stories.py from the committed
# case JSONs. Like web/metro/ and web/go/, absent from a fresh checkout.
web/stories/
web/methodology/

# Per-ZIP velocity payloads — the PAID layer. Served only through
# verify-access (Supabase); committing them would publish the paid feature in
# a public repo. The aggregate velocity-{month}.json files ARE committed.
pipeline/velocity/zip-velocity-latest.json

# Raw Redfin sources cached by tools/backtest_cases.py (~1GB). The COMPUTED
# case JSONs in web/data/cases/ are committed; their inputs are not.
.cache/

# Read-only exposure audit — names every sensitive path and commit in one
# place. Kept local; publishing it would publish the map.
AUDIT_REPORT.md
# LICENSE_AUDIT.md names an exposure that is still OPEN — the exact URL of a
# live per-ZIP file, the row count, and the fact that no gate catches it. The
# sibling audits (PURGE_MANIFEST, HISTORY_SCRUB_NOTES, ABSENCE_TEST_AUDIT) are
# tracked because what they describe is finished. This repo is public; a
# roadmap to an open hole is not something to publish alongside the hole.
LICENSE_AUDIT.md

# GITHUB_PURGE_REQUEST.md lists the exact commit SHAs by which the withdrawn
# data is STILL retrievable from GitHub — that is the whole point of the
# request. Committing it to a public repo would publish a working index to the
# objects we are asking to have deleted, turning a request to make data harder
# to find into a document that makes it easier. It goes in the support ticket,
# not the repo. Remove this line once GitHub confirms the GC is complete and
# the SHAs point at nothing.
GITHUB_PURGE_REQUEST.md
.build/

# GITHUB_TICKET_PAUSE_REPLY.md records WHY the GC request was paused — that a
# licence question is open and being taken elsewhere. Same reason as the two
# entries above: this repo is public, and the reasoning is not for it. The
# dated fact that the request is paused lives in REMEDIATION_DATES.md; the
# reasoning does not.
GITHUB_TICKET_PAUSE_REPLY.md

# DERIVED_USE_INVENTORY.md is a lineage map of everything with the former
# vendor's data in its computation chain, and it names exposures that are still
# OPEN — including per-ZIP rating data reachable from this repository while the
# site says it is not published. Same reason as LICENSE_AUDIT.md above: this
# repository is public, and a register of open holes does not belong in it.
# It goes to counsel directly. LEGAL_HOLD.md rule 3 refers to it by name.
DERIVED_USE_INVENTORY.md

# Dated captures of vendor terms-of-use pages. Kept out of the public repo:
# they are third-party content, and the point of holding them is the private
# record of what the terms said on a date, not republication.
# snapshot_vendor_terms.py refuses to write anywhere git does not ignore.
docs/vendor-terms
# No trailing slash on purpose: a `dir/` pattern only matches a directory
# that already EXISTS, so `git check-ignore` said "not ignored" on a fresh
# CI checkout and snapshot_vendor_terms.py refused to write. Verified 2026-08-23.

# Per-ZIP research state. Moved to public.research_state (schema-v40) on
# 2026-08-23 and removed from this repository, which is public: these files
# published ~25,000 ZIP-to-rating pairs a month, roughly 20,000 of them for
# markets whose own pages decline to state a rating, while the release page
# said "We do not publish the list".
#
# They are still WRITTEN locally as a cache — research.save_levels dual-writes —
# so a machine that has run a build keeps working without credentials. The store
# is the source of truth; CI reads it and has no copy of these.
# Verified before removal: --verify-store recomputed July's flip count as 2,403
# from the store alone, with the files unreachable.
pipeline/research/levels-*.json
pipeline/research/streaks.json

# Counsel drafts and the dated verification behind them. Same reason as
# LICENSE_AUDIT.md and DERIVED_USE_INVENTORY.md: this repository is public and
# these describe open questions, not settled ones.
SUPPLEMENT_2_DRAFT.md
ARCHIVE_VERIFICATION_*.md
